# SEO context

Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Supabase. English-language travel blog.
Admin CMS at `/admin/articles/[id]/edit`, custom Notion-style block editor on TipTap.

## Relevant existing pieces

- `app/` — App Router
- `components/admin/NotionArticlePage.tsx` — page shell, autosave, publish
- `components/admin/NotionEditor/PropertyRow.tsx` — article metadata fields UI
- `components/public/article-block-view.tsx` — public renderer, react-markdown
- `lib/blocks/types.ts` — ArticleBlock, Article types
- `supabase/migrations/` — convention: `20260712210000_name.sql`
- Supabase table `articles`, body in `content` JSONB, `lang` defaults to `en`

Server Actions: `autosaveArticle` (debounced), `saveArticle` (publish).
Revisions: `lib/article-revisions.ts`.

## Hard constraints

1. INSPECT THE EXISTING SCHEMA FIRST. Read the latest migrations and the Article type before writing any SQL. Add only columns that do not already exist.
2. Do not break autosave. Any new column must be nullable or have a default, and existing rows must be backfilled in the same migration.
3. Do not change the shape of `content` JSONB or the ArticleBlock union.
4. The site is English only. Do NOT add hreflang, locale routing, or i18n scaffolding.
5. Metadata must be server-rendered. Never set title, description or canonical from a client component or a useEffect.
6. Detect the current rendering strategy of the public article route (static, ISR, or dynamic) and adapt rather than converting it.
7. Every new admin field goes through PropertyRow's existing popover pattern. Do not introduce a second settings UI.
